#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:15
msgid "Excalidraw Diagram Skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:17
msgid ""
"Create diagrams by writing standard Excalidraw element JSON and saving as"
" `.excalidraw` files. These files can be drag-and-dropped onto "
"[excalidraw.com](https://excalidraw.com) for viewing and editing. No "
"accounts, no API keys, no rendering libraries -- just JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:19
msgid "Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:21
msgid "**Load this skill** (you already did)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:22
msgid "**Write the elements JSON** -- an array of Excalidraw element objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:23
msgid "**Save the file** using `write_file` to create a `.excalidraw` file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"**Optionally upload** for a shareable link using `scripts/upload.py` via "
"`terminal`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:26
msgid "Saving a Diagram"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:28
msgid ""
"Wrap your elements array in the standard `.excalidraw` envelope and save "
"with `write_file`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:42
msgid "Save to any path, e.g. `~/diagrams/my_diagram.excalidraw`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:44
msgid "Uploading for a Shareable Link"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:46
msgid ""
"Run the upload script (located in this skill's `scripts/` directory) via "
"terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:52
msgid ""
"This uploads to excalidraw.com (no account needed) and prints a shareable"
" URL. Requires the `cryptography` pip package (`pip install "
"cryptography`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:56
msgid "Element Format Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:58
msgid "Required Fields (all elements)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:59
msgid "`type`, `id` (unique string), `x`, `y`, `width`, `height`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:61
msgid "Defaults (skip these -- they're applied automatically)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:62
msgid "`strokeColor`: `\"#1e1e1e\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:63
msgid "`backgroundColor`: `\"transparent\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:64
msgid "`fillStyle`: `\"solid\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:65
msgid "`strokeWidth`: `2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:66
msgid "`roughness`: `1` (hand-drawn look)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:67
msgid "`opacity`: `100`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:69
msgid "Canvas background is white."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:71
msgid "Element Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:73
msgid "**Rectangle**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:77
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`roundness: { \"type\": 3 }` for rounded corners"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:78
msgid "`backgroundColor: \"#a5d8ff\"`, `fillStyle: \"solid\"` for filled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:80
msgid "**Ellipse**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:85
msgid "**Diamond**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:90
msgid ""
"**Labeled shape (container binding)** -- create a text element bound to "
"the shape:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:92
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**WARNING:** Do NOT use `\"label\": { \"text\": \"...\" }` on shapes. "
"This is NOT a valid Excalidraw property and will be silently ignored, "
"producing blank shapes. You MUST use the container binding approach "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:96
msgid ""
"The shape needs `boundElements` listing the text, and the text needs "
"`containerId` pointing back:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:106
msgid "Works on rectangle, ellipse, diamond"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:107
msgid "Text is auto-centered by Excalidraw when `containerId` is set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:108
msgid ""
"The text `x`/`y`/`width`/`height` are approximate -- Excalidraw "
"recalculates them on load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:109
msgid "`originalText` should match `text`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:110
msgid "Always include `fontFamily: 1` (Virgil/hand-drawn font)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:112
msgid "**Labeled arrow** -- same container binding approach:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:123
msgid "**Standalone text** (titles and annotations only -- no container):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:128
msgid ""
"`x` is the LEFT edge. To center at position `cx`: `x = cx - (text.length "
"* fontSize * 0.5) / 2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:129
msgid "Do NOT rely on `textAlign` or `width` for positioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:131
msgid "**Arrow**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:136
msgid "`points`: `[dx, dy]` offsets from element `x`, `y`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:137
msgid ""
"`endArrowhead`: `null` | `\"arrow\"` | `\"bar\"` | `\"dot\"` | "
"`\"triangle\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:138
msgid "`strokeStyle`: `\"solid\"` (default) | `\"dashed\"` | `\"dotted\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:140
msgid "Arrow Bindings (connect arrows to shapes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:151
msgid ""
"`fixedPoint` coordinates: `top=[0.5,0]`, `bottom=[0.5,1]`, "
"`left=[0,0.5]`, `right=[1,0.5]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:153
msgid "Drawing Order (z-order)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:154
msgid "Array order = z-order (first = back, last = front)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:155
msgid ""
"Emit progressively: background zones → shape → its bound text → its "
"arrows → next shape"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:156
msgid "BAD: all rectangles, then all texts, then all arrows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:157
msgid ""
"GOOD: bg_zone → shape1 → text_for_shape1 → arrow1 → arrow_label_text → "
"shape2 → text_for_shape2 → ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/excalidraw_SKILL.md:158
msgid "Always place the bound text element immediately after its container shape"
msgstr ""

